  "question": "1) Background / Context\n\nThe project involves the development of a system for collecting and managing airline on-time performance data. This data is reported monthly to the U.S. Department of Transportation (DOT), Bureau of Transportation Statistics (BTS) by selected U.S. air carriers. The goal is to store, manage, and analyze data related to flight times, delays, cancellations, and diversions for statistical and reporting purposes.\n\n 2) Objectives\n\n- To establish a robust database system that captures and stores detailed information about airline performance.\n- To facilitate the analysis and reporting of airline on-time performance for regulatory compliance and public information.\n- To manage various classifications and codes related to airports, carriers, and delays.\n\n 3) Stakeholders & Users\n\n- U.S. Department of Transportation (DOT)\n- Bureau of Transportation Statistics (BTS)\n- Airline companies\n- Data analysts and researchers\n- Regulatory bodies\n\n 4) Functional Descriptions\n\n- Data Collection: Capture and store data related to flight schedules, delays, cancellations, and diversions.\n- Data Management: Utilize tables to manage codes and descriptions for airlines, airports, delay reasons, and more.\n- Analytics Support: Provide data structures to support analysis on flight performance and delay causes.\n- Reporting: Generate reports detailing on-time performance metrics for regulatory and public dissemination.\n\n 5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Performance: Support large volumes of data with efficient querying and data retrieval.\n- Reliability: Ensure data accuracy and consistency across different data entries and reports.\n- Scalability: Accommodate data increase over time as the number of airlines and flights grow.\n- Security: Protect sensitive data with appropriate access controls and authentication mechanisms.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0090\nCREATE TABLE `airline` (\n  `airline_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `carrier_code` char(2) NOT NULL,\n  `carrier_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`airline_id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `carrier_code` (`carrier_code`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `airport` (\n  `airport_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `airport_code` char(3) NOT NULL,\n  `airport_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `city_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `state_code` char(2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`airport_id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `airport_code` (`airport_code`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `delay_reason` (\n  `delay_reason_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `delay_code` char(2) NOT NULL,\n  `delay_description` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`delay_reason_id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `delay_code` (`delay_code`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `flight_performance` (\n  `flight_performance_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `report_year` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `report_month` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `carrier_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `flight_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `flight_number` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `origin_airport_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `destination_airport_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `scheduled_departure_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `actual_departure_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `scheduled_arrival_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `actual_arrival_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `departure_delay_minutes` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `arrival_delay_minutes` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `cancelled_flag` char(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'N',\n  `diverted_flag` char(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'N',\n  `delay_reason_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `reporting_source` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`flight_performance_id`),\n  KEY `carrier_id` (`carrier_id`),\n  KEY `origin_airport_id` (`origin_airport_id`),\n  KEY `destination_airport_id` (`destination_airport_id`),\n  KEY `delay_reason_id` (`delay_reason_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `flight_performance_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`carrier_id`) REFERENCES `airline` (`airline_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `flight_performance_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`origin_airport_id`) REFERENCES `airport` (`airport_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `flight_performance_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`destination_airport_id`) REFERENCES `airport` (`airport_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `flight_performance_ibfk_4` FOREIGN KEY (`delay_reason_id`) REFERENCES `delay_reason` (`delay_reason_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
